# Cloudflare's header rules for the site's files (docs/decisions/2026-10-21-cloudflare-for-the-site.md).
# Vite names every file under /assets/ by its content's hash, so a file
# there never changes: a year, and the browser never asks again. Everything
# else keeps Cloudflare's default (asked again each visit, a 304 when it's
# unchanged), as its name stays the same when it changes. Rules that match
# one path are merged, a header set twice joined with a comma: so no rule
# for /* sets Cache-Control. (GitHub Pages serves this as a plain file and
# applies none of it.)
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Any site may read the files, as GitHub Pages lets it (it sends this on
# every file): the Minecraft player, on an origin of its own, fetches the
# game's sealed file from /eagler/ (public/eagler-player/index.html), and
# without it the game wouldn't open once the domain is Cloudflare's. A
# public site with no logins: nothing is given away. (A file there stays
# under Cloudflare's 25 MiB: 1.12.2.bin is 22.2.)
/*
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
